• Similar techniques were later used in technologies such as Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.

The student wants to emphasize the lasting influence of Lamarr's invention.$q$,$q$Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$,$j$["During World War II, Hedy Lamarr co-invented a frequency-hopping system.","Frequency hopping was designed to prevent radio signals from being jammed.","Hedy Lamarr's frequency-hopping invention used techniques similar to those later found in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth.","Hedy Lamarr was a film actress in the 1930s and 1940s."]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Connecting the invention to later Wi-Fi and Bluetooth technology shows its lasting influence.$q$,$j${"0":"This names the invention but says nothing about its later influence."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000054','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',2,$q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
• Mount Everest is 8,849 meters tall.
