• Measured from its base on the ocean floor, Mauna Kea is about 10,200 meters tall.

The student wants to contrast how the two mountains' heights compare depending on how height is measured.$q$,$q$Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$,$j$["Mount Everest is 8,849 meters tall, and Mauna Kea is in Hawaii.","Mauna Kea rises 4,207 meters above sea level.","Mount Everest is taller above sea level, but measured from its base on the ocean floor, Mauna Kea is taller.","Both Mount Everest and Mauna Kea are mountains, and both are very tall."]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$This choice directly contrasts the two measurements: Everest wins above sea level, Mauna Kea wins base to peak.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000055','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',3,$q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
