The student wants to emphasize that penicillin's discovery was accidental.$q$,$q$Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$,$j$["Fleming discovered penicillin after mold happened to contaminate a bacteria culture and killed the nearby bacteria.","In 1928, Fleming named a substance produced by mold \"penicillin.\"","Penicillin was not mass-produced as a medicine until the 1940s.","Penicillin, discovered in 1928, later became a mass-produced medicine."]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$Describing the mold as having "happened to contaminate" the culture emphasizes the accident behind the discovery.$q$,$j${"3":"This summarizes the timeline but doesn't convey that the discovery was accidental."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000056','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',3,$q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
