The student wants to present the study's finding to an audience unfamiliar with the research.$q$,$q$Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$,$j$["Researchers compared two groups of students learning vocabulary.","Group A studied in one long session, while Group B studied over a week.","Group B remembered significantly more words than Group A.","In one study, students who spread their vocabulary practice over several shorter sessions remembered more words a month later than students who studied in one long session."]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$For an unfamiliar audience, the sentence must explain the groups and the result in plain terms, not refer to labels like "Group B."$q$,$j${"2":"\"Group A\" and \"Group B\" mean nothing to someone unfamiliar with the study."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000057','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',3,$q$The Nile River flooded predictably each year, depositing rich silt on the surrounding fields. Ancient Egyptian farmers planted their crops as the waters receded. ______ they developed one of the earliest known calendars, which helped them anticipate the flood.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$,$j$["By contrast,","To track this cycle,","In other words,","Despite this pattern,"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$The calendar was developed to anticipate the yearly flood, so a purpose transition linking it to the cycle fits best.$q$,$j${"3":"The calendar wasn't developed in spite of the pattern; it was developed because of it."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000058','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',3,$q$Electric cars produce no tailpipe emissions. ______ their overall environmental impact depends partly on how the electricity that charges them is generated; cars charged from coal-fired plants are associated with more emissions than those charged from solar or wind power.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$,$j$["Still,","For this reason,","Accordingly,","Therefore,"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$The second sentence qualifies the first — despite no tailpipe emissions, impact depends on the power source — so a concessive contrast fits.$q$,$j${"3":"The second sentence isn't a conclusion drawn from the first."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000059','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',1,$q$Penguins cannot fly. ______ they are excellent swimmers, using their wings as flippers to move quickly through the water.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?$q$,$j$["However,","For example,","Therefore,","Similarly,"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$Being excellent swimmers contrasts with being unable to fly.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000060','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-expression-ideas',2,$q$While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:
