The student wants to stress how much marine life is supported by a small area of ocean.$q$,$q$Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?$q$,$j$["About 25% of marine species depend on coral reefs, which may be killed by bleaching.","Although coral reefs cover less than 1% of the ocean floor, about 25% of all marine species depend on them.","Rising ocean temperatures can cause coral bleaching.","Coral reefs cover less than 1% of the ocean floor and face threats from warming waters."]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$This choice pairs the small area (less than 1%) with the large share of species (25%), which is exactly the contrast the student wants.$q$,$j${"0":"This mentions the share of species but not the small area."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000066','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$The collection of rare maps ______ displayed in the library's east wing.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["were","is","are","have been"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$The subject is "collection" (singular), not "maps," so the singular verb "is" is correct.$q$,$j${"2":"\"Maps\" is part of a prepositional phrase; the subject is \"collection.\""}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000067','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$Each of the students in the robotics club ______ a different part of the competition robot.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["are designing","design","have designed","designs"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$"Each" is singular, so it takes the singular verb "designs."$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000068','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$The orchestra performed three pieces at the festival ______ a symphony, a concerto, and a short overture.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$[",",":",";","—and"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$A colon correctly introduces a list after a complete independent clause.$q$,$j${"2":"A semicolon must join two independent clauses; the list isn't one."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000069','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$Marisol finished her research paper two days ______ the extra time revising it carefully.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["early she spent","early. She spent","early, she spent","early, she, spent"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$These are two independent clauses, so they must be separated as two sentences (or joined with a semicolon). A comma alone creates a comma splice.$q$,$j${"0":"With no punctuation, this is a run-on sentence.","2":"A comma alone between two independent clauses is a comma splice."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000070','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$The company announced that ______ new headquarters would open in the spring.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["it's","its","their","its'"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$"Company" is singular and the word shows possession, so "its" is correct.$q$,$j${"0":"\"It's\" means \"it is.\"","2":"\"Company\" is singular, so use \"its,\" not \"their.\""}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000071','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$Walking through the botanical garden, ______$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["the visitors admired the rare orchids.","admiration for the rare orchids grew.","the orchids, which were rare, were admired.","the rare orchids impressed the visitors."]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$The opening phrase describes who was walking, so it must be followed by "the visitors." Otherwise the modifier dangles.$q$,$j${"3":"This says the orchids were walking through the garden."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000072','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$The novelist ______ books have been translated into more than forty languages, rarely gives interviews.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["whom","who's","which","whose"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$"Whose" shows possession (the novelist's books).$q$,$j${"1":"\"Who's\" means \"who is.\""}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000073','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$In 1969, Apollo 11 astronauts Neil Armstrong and Buzz ______ became the first people to walk on the Moon.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["Aldrin","Aldrin;","Aldrin,","Aldrin—"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$No punctuation is needed between the subject "Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin" and the verb "became."$q$,$j${"2":"A comma shouldn't separate a subject from its verb."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000074','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$The city's oldest bridge, built in 1889 ______ still carries thousands of cars each day.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["—",";",":",","]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$The phrase "built in 1889" is set off by a comma before it, so it must be closed with a matching comma.$q$,$j${"0":"A dash can't close a phrase that a comma opened."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000075','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$Neither the coach nor the players ______ expecting the storm to delay the game.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["was","were","has been","is"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$With "neither … nor," the verb agrees with the nearer subject, "players," which is plural.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000076','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',3,$q$The research team, which included biologists, chemists, and ______ spent three years studying the effects of the pollutant.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["engineers","engineers,","engineers;","engineers:"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$The nonessential clause "which included…" began with a comma after "team," so it must end with a comma before the verb "spent."$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000077','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',3,$q$Many of the earliest photographs required long exposure ______ subjects had to remain perfectly still for several minutes, which is why so few people in early portraits are smiling.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["times, and so,","times;","times","times,"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$"Many…required long exposure times" and "subjects had to remain…still" are independent clauses; a semicolon joins them correctly.$q$,$j${"3":"A comma alone would create a comma splice."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000078','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',3,$q$By the time the rescue team arrived, the hikers ______ for nearly two days.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["have been waiting","waits","had been waiting","will have waited"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The waiting happened before another past event (the team's arrival), so the past perfect progressive "had been waiting" is correct.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000079','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',3,$q$Biologist Rachel Carson's 1962 book Silent ______ documented the harmful effects of pesticides and helped launch the modern environmental movement.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["Spring","Spring—",", Spring,","Spring,"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$The title is essential to identify which book is meant, so no commas set it off, and no punctuation separates it from the verb.$q$,$j${"3":"A comma here would separate the subject from its verb."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000080','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$The students' science projects ______ judged by a panel of local engineers.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["was","is","were","has been"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$"Projects" is plural, so the plural verb "were" is correct.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000081','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$Each spring, thousands of sandhill cranes stop along the Platte River in ______ they rest and feed before continuing north.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["Nebraska where","Nebraska, where","Nebraska. Where","Nebraska; where"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$"Where they rest…" is a dependent clause that adds information, so it's set off with a comma.$q$,$j${"2":"\"Where they rest and feed before continuing north\" can't stand alone as a sentence."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000082','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$The museum's director, along with two curators, ______ the new exhibit this morning.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["were presenting","have presented","is presenting","are presenting"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The subject is "director"; "along with two curators" doesn't make it plural.$q$,$j${"3":"\"Along with\" phrases don't change a singular subject to plural."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000083','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$Having trained for months in the summer heat, ______$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["the coaches considered the marathon an easy race.","the marathon was easier for the runners than expected.","the runners were well prepared for the marathon.","preparation for the marathon was complete."]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The opening phrase describes people who trained, so it must be followed by the people who did the training: "the runners."$q$,$j${"0":"The runners trained, not the coaches.","1":"This says the marathon trained for months."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000084','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',3,$q$Both of the ______ reports reached the same conclusion: the bridge needed repairs within five years.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["engineers'","engineers's","engineers","engineer's"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$Two engineers wrote reports ("both"), so the plural possessive "engineers'" is correct.$q$,$j${"3":"\"Both\" indicates more than one engineer, so the singular possessive doesn't fit."}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000085','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',3,$q$The scientist explained that the samples ______ collected from three different depths, which allowed the team to compare conditions across the water column.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["has been","was","had been","is"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The plural subject "samples" needs a plural verb, and the collection happened before the explanation, so "had been" is correct.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000086','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',2,$q$Jazz musician Mary Lou Williams composed hundreds of ______ arranged music for bandleaders such as Duke Ellington and Benny Goodman.$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["works, and,","works and","works. And","works; and"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$"Composed…and arranged" is a compound verb with one subject; no comma or semicolon should separate the two verbs.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b020000-0000-4000-8000-000000000087','SAT',$q$Reading and Writing$q$,'sat-conventions',1,$q$My grandmother's garden has roses, tulips, and ______$q$,$q$Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?$q$,$j$["daisys.","daisy's.","daisies'.","daisies."]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$The plural of "daisy" is "daisies," and no possession is shown.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,71,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b030000-0001-4000-8000-000000000001','ACT',$q$English$q$,'act-eng-rhetoric',1,$q$Passage I — Reviving the Lot on Alder Street
For years, the empty lot on Alder Street was __a place that was full and crowded with__ weeds, broken glass, and an abandoned shopping cart. Most neighbors walked past it without a second glance, my aunt Rosa saw something different. She had grown up on a farm, and they imagined rows of tomatoes and beans where the trash now lay.

In the spring of 2019, Rosa organizes a meeting at the community center. Only six people came. Therefore, they left with a plan: they would ask the city for permission to use the lot, and they would clean it themselves.

The cleanup took three weekends. Volunteers hauled away two hundred bags' of trash, tested the soil, and built twelve raised beds out of donated lumber. By the following summer, the garden had a waiting list of families eager for a plot.

Today the garden grow more than vegetables. Children learn where food comes from, older residents trade recipes, and neighbors who once had barely known each other now share tools and advice. Rosa likes to say that the garden's best harvest have been friendship.$q$,$q$Which choice is best for the underlined portion?$q$,$j$["NO CHANGE","full of","a location that contained within it","filled up and full with"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$"Full of" says the same thing without the wordiness of the other choices.$q$,$j${"0":"The original repeats the same idea (full, crowded) and adds unnecessary words."}$j$::jsonb,42,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
