('5b030000-0004-4000-8000-000000000035','ACT',$q$English$q$,'act-eng-conventions',1,$q$Passage IV — Helping the Monarchs
Each fall, millions of monarch butterflies __migrates__ from Canada and the northern United States to the mountains of central Mexico, a journey, of up to 3,000 miles. No single butterfly makes the entire round trip; it takes several generation's for the population to return north.

Fortunately, the eastern monarch population has declined sharply since the 1990s. Scientists point to several different multiple causes, including the loss of milkweed, the only plant on which monarch caterpillars can feed. As farms and suburbs have expanded, milkweed has disappeared from much of the monarchs' range.

Volunteers across the continent are trying to help. Schools plant milkweed gardens, and highway departments let roadside plants grow instead of mowing them. Citizen scientists tag butterflies with small stickers, allowing researchers to track where individual monarchs travel.

Whether these efforts will be enough remains uncertain. But for many volunteers, the work is its own reward: few sights compare to a garden full of orange wings in late summer?$q$,$q$Which choice is best for the underlined portion?$q$,$j$["NO CHANGE","has migrated","migrate","migrating"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The plural subject "butterflies" requires the plural verb "migrate."$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,42,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
