('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$What is the value of 3x² − 2x when x = −3?$q$,$j$["−33","21","33","39"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$3(−3)² − 2(−3) = 27 + 6 = 33.$q$,$j${"1":"Subtracting 2(−3) means adding 6, not subtracting it."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$What value of x satisfies 7x − 4 = 3x + 20?$q$,$j$["4","5","6","24"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Subtract 3x and add 4: 4x = 24, so x = 6.$q$,$j${"3":"24 is the value of 4x."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$A shirt costs $18.00, and the sales tax rate is 6%. What is the total cost of the shirt, including tax?$q$,$j$["$18.06","$19.08","$19.80","$24.00"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$Tax is 0.06 × 18 = $1.08, so the total is $19.08.$q$,$j${"0":"This adds 6 cents instead of 6%."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$What is the median of the data set 8, 3, 11, 5, 7?$q$,$j$["6.8","7","8","11"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$In order: 3, 5, 7, 8, 11. The middle value is 7.$q$,$j${"0":"6.8 is the mean.","2":"Order the values first; 8 is not the middle one."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$If f(x) = 4x + 9, what is f(−5)?$q$,$j$["−20","−11","11","29"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$f(−5) = 4(−5) + 9 = −20 + 9 = −11.$q$,$j${"3":"4(−5) is −20, not +20."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$Which expression is equivalent to 3(2x − 5) − 4x?$q$,$j$["2x + 15","2x − 5","10x − 15","2x − 15"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$Distribute: 6x − 15 − 4x = 2x − 15.$q$,$j${"1":"Distribute the 3 to both terms inside the parentheses."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',1,null,$q$The ratio of boys to girls in a class is 3:5. If the class has 32 students, how many are girls?$q$,$j$["12","15","18","20"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$There are 3 + 5 = 8 parts, so each part is 32 ÷ 8 = 4 students. Girls: 5 × 4 = 20.$q$,$j${"0":"12 is the number of boys."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$What is the slope of the line through the points (−2, 7) and (4, −5)?$q$,$j$["−2","−1/2","1/2","2"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$Slope = (−5 − 7)/(4 − (−2)) = −12/6 = −2.$q$,$j${"1":"This divides the run by the rise."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$What are the solutions of x² − 3x − 28 = 0?$q$,$j$["x = 4 and x = −7","x = −4 and x = −7","x = 4 and x = 7","x = −4 and x = 7"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$Factor: (x − 7)(x + 4) = 0, so x = 7 or x = −4.$q$,$j${"0":"Check by substituting: 4² − 3(4) − 28 ≠ 0."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000010','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$A car rental costs $40 per day plus $0.25 per mile driven. Lee rented a car for 3 days and paid $165. How many miles did Lee drive?$q$,$j$["125","180","500","660"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$The daily charge is 3 × $40 = $120, leaving $45 for miles. $45 ÷ $0.25 = 180 miles.$q$,$j${"2":"This charges only one day.","3":"This ignores the daily charge."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$What is the value of |−8 + 3| − |4 − 10|?$q$,$j$["−11","−1","1","11"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$|−5| − |−6| = 5 − 6 = −1.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$If 2ˣ = 32, what is the value of 2ˣ⁻²?$q$,$j$["3","8","16","30"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$2ˣ⁻² = 2ˣ ÷ 2² = 32 ÷ 4 = 8.$q$,$j${"0":"3 is the value of x − 2.","3":"Subtracting 2 from the exponent divides by 4; it doesn't subtract 2."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000013','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$The average of Kim's 4 test scores is 85. What score must she earn on a fifth test to raise her average to 87?$q$,$j$["87","89","93","95"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$She needs a total of 5 × 87 = 435. She has 4 × 85 = 340, so she needs 95.$q$,$j${"1":"Raising the average by 2 points across 5 tests requires much more than 2 extra points."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$Which inequality is equivalent to −3x + 5 ≤ 17?$q$,$j$["x ≥ 4","x ≤ 4","x ≤ −4","x ≥ −4"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$Subtract 5: −3x ≤ 12. Divide by −3 and reverse the sign: x ≥ −4.$q$,$j${"2":"Dividing by a negative number reverses the inequality."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$An integer from 1 through 20 is chosen at random. What is the probability that it is a multiple of 3 or a multiple of 5?$q$,$j$["3/10","2/5","9/20","1/2"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Multiples of 3: 6 numbers. Multiples of 5: 4 numbers. 15 is counted twice, so there are 6 + 4 − 1 = 9 favorable outcomes.$q$,$j${"3":"This counts 15 twice."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$If g(x) = x² + 1 and h(x) = 2x − 3, what is g(h(2))?$q$,$j$["2","5","7","10"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$h(2) = 2(2) − 3 = 1, and g(1) = 1² + 1 = 2.$q$,$j${"1":"5 is g(2), before applying h.","2":"7 is h(g(2)) — the functions are applied in the wrong order."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000017','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$Which expression is equivalent to (3x²y)(4xy³)?$q$,$j$["12x²y³","12x³y⁴","12x³y³","7x³y⁴"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$Multiply coefficients (3 × 4 = 12) and add exponents of like bases: x²⁺¹ = x³, y¹⁺³ = y⁴.$q$,$j${"3":"Multiply the coefficients; don't add them."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000018','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$For what value of a does the system ax + 2y = 7 and 6x + 4y = 9 have no solution?$q$,$j$["2","3","6","12"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$No solution means parallel lines: a/6 = 2/4, so a = 3. (The constants 7 and 9 aren't in the same ratio, so the lines are distinct.)$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000019','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$The sum of three consecutive odd integers is 87. What is the largest of the three integers?$q$,$j$["27","29","31","33"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Let the integers be n, n + 2, n + 4: 3n + 6 = 87, so n = 27. The largest is 31.$q$,$j${"0":"27 is the smallest.","1":"29 is the middle integer."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000020','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$If log₂ x = 5, what is the value of x?$q$,$j$["2.5","10","25","32"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$log₂ x = 5 means 2⁵ = x, so x = 32.$q$,$j${"1":"This multiplies 2 by 5 instead of raising 2 to the 5th power."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$A geometric sequence has a first term of 3 and a common ratio of 2. What is the 8th term?$q$,$j$["48","192","384","768"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The nth term is 3 · 2ⁿ⁻¹, so the 8th term is 3 · 2⁷ = 3 · 128 = 384.$q$,$j${"3":"768 is the 9th term."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000022','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',2,null,$q$For which value of x is the function f(x) = (x + 2)/(x − 5) undefined?$q$,$j$["−5","−2","2","5"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$The function is undefined when the denominator is zero: x − 5 = 0, so x = 5.$q$,$j${"1":"At x = −2 the function equals 0; it's still defined."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000023','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$What is the sum of the solutions of 2x² − 10x + 7 = 0?$q$,$j$["−5","7/2","5","10"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$For ax² + bx + c = 0, the sum of the solutions is −b/a = 10/2 = 5.$q$,$j${"1":"7/2 is the product of the solutions (c/a)."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000024','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$For i = √−1, which expression is equivalent to (3 + 2i)(1 − i)?$q$,$j$["5 − i","3 − 2i","5 + i","1 − i"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$3 − 3i + 2i − 2i² = 3 − i + 2 = 5 − i, since i² = −1.$q$,$j${"3":"−2i² is +2, not −2."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000025','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-algebra',3,null,$q$An account earns 3% interest compounded annually. Which expression gives the balance, in dollars, after 10 years if $500 is deposited and nothing is withdrawn?$q$,$j$["500(0.03)¹⁰","500(1.3)¹⁰","500(1.03)¹⁰","500 + 0.03(10)"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Each year the balance is multiplied by 1.03, so after 10 years it's 500(1.03)¹⁰.$q$,$j${"1":"1.3 would be 30% interest."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000026','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$The perimeter of a square is 36 inches. What is the area of the square, in square inches?$q$,$j$["9","36","81","144"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Each side is 36 ÷ 4 = 9 inches, so the area is 9² = 81.$q$,$j${"0":"9 is the side length."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000027','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$Two angles of a triangle measure 35° and 90°. What is the measure of the third angle?$q$,$j$["45°","55°","65°","145°"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$180 − 35 − 90 = 55.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000028','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$What is the circumference of a circle with a diameter of 10 centimeters?$q$,$j$["10π cm","100π cm","5π cm","25π cm"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$Circumference = π × diameter = π(10) = 10π centimeters.$q$,$j${"3":"25π is the area."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000029','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$What is the distance between the points (1, 2) and (4, 6) in the standard (x, y) coordinate plane?$q$,$j$["5","25","7","√7"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$√((4 − 1)² + (6 − 2)²) = √(9 + 16) = 5.$q$,$j${"2":"7 adds the horizontal and vertical distances instead of using the Pythagorean theorem."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000030','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$A rectangle has an area of 48 square meters and a length of 8 meters. What is its perimeter, in meters?$q$,$j$["14","28","40","56"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$Width = 48 ÷ 8 = 6. Perimeter = 2(8 + 6) = 28.$q$,$j${"0":"14 is half the perimeter."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000031','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$What is the midpoint of the segment with endpoints (−3, 4) and (5, 10)?$q$,$j$["(2, 14)","(4, 3)","(8, 6)","(1, 7)"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$Average the coordinates: ((−3 + 5)/2, (4 + 10)/2) = (1, 7).$q$,$j${"0":"This adds the coordinates without dividing by 2."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000032','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',1,null,$q$Two angles are supplementary, and one angle measures 4 times the other. What is the measure of the larger angle?$q$,$j$["36°","72°","135°","144°"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$x + 4x = 180, so x = 36 and the larger angle is 144°.$q$,$j${"0":"36° is the smaller angle."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000033','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$A right triangle has legs of length 9 and 12. What is the length of the hypotenuse?$q$,$j$["√63","21","15","225"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$√(81 + 144) = √225 = 15.$q$,$j${"3":"225 is the hypotenuse squared."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000034','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$In a right triangle, the side opposite angle θ has length 7 and the hypotenuse has length 25. What is cos θ?$q$,$j$["7/25","7/24","24/25","25/24"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The adjacent side is √(625 − 49) = 24, so cos θ = adjacent/hypotenuse = 24/25.$q$,$j${"0":"7/25 is sin θ."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000035','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$A trapezoid has bases of 10 and 16 inches and a height of 5 inches. What is its area, in square inches?$q$,$j$["31","65","80","130"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$A = (1/2)(b₁ + b₂)h = (1/2)(26)(5) = 65.$q$,$j${"3":"Don't forget the 1/2."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000036','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$What is the volume of a sphere with a radius of 3 units? (V = (4/3)πr³)$q$,$j$["27π","108π","12π","36π"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$(4/3)π(27) = 36π.$q$,$j${"1":"108π leaves out the 1/3."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000037','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$A line in the standard (x, y) coordinate plane passes through the origin and is perpendicular to the line y = −3x + 7. What is its equation?$q$,$j$["y = −(1/3)x","y = −3x","y = 3x","y = (1/3)x"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$The perpendicular slope is the negative reciprocal of −3, which is 1/3. Passing through the origin gives y = (1/3)x.$q$,$j${"1":"This line is parallel, not perpendicular."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000038','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$What is the measure of each interior angle of a regular hexagon?$q$,$j$["60°","108°","120°","135°"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Interior angle sum = (6 − 2)180 = 720°. Each of the 6 angles is 120°.$q$,$j${"0":"60° is the exterior angle.","1":"108° is the interior angle of a regular pentagon."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000039','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$A 13-foot ladder leans against a vertical wall with its base 5 feet from the wall on level ground. How high up the wall does the ladder reach, in feet?$q$,$j$["18","8","12","√194"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$5² + h² = 13², so h² = 144 and h = 12.$q$,$j${"3":"The ladder is the hypotenuse; subtract, don't add, the squares."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000040','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$Which equation describes the circle with center (2, −1) and radius 4?$q$,$j$["(x − 2)² + (y + 1)² = 16","(x + 2)² + (y − 1)² = 16","(x + 2)² + (y − 1)² = 4","(x − 2)² + (y + 1)² = 4"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$(x − h)² + (y − k)² = r² with (h, k) = (2, −1) and r² = 16.$q$,$j${"3":"The right side is r², not r."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000041','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',2,null,$q$A 6-foot-tall person casts a 4-foot shadow at the same time that a tree casts a 30-foot shadow. How tall is the tree, in feet?$q$,$j$["20","32","45","180"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The ratio of height to shadow is 6:4 = 1.5, so the tree is 1.5 × 30 = 45 feet.$q$,$j${"0":"This inverts the ratio."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000042','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$What is the area of a sector of a circle with radius 12 and a central angle of 60°?$q$,$j$["72π","24π","12π","4π"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$(60/360)π(12²) = (1/6)(144π) = 24π.$q$,$j${"3":"4π is the arc length."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000043','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$If sin θ = 3/5 and θ is in Quadrant II, what is tan θ?$q$,$j$["−4/3","−3/4","3/4","4/3"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$In Quadrant II, cos θ is negative: cos θ = −4/5. tan θ = sin θ / cos θ = −3/4.$q$,$j${"2":"Tangent is negative in Quadrant II."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000044','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$A rectangular box measures 2 by 3 by 6 inches. What is the length of the longest segment that fits inside the box (its space diagonal), in inches?$q$,$j$["7","6","√13","11"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$√(2² + 3² + 6²) = √49 = 7.$q$,$j${"3":"11 adds the dimensions."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000045','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$A triangle has side lengths 7, 24, and 25. What is its area?$q$,$j$["84","87.5","168","300"]$j$::jsonb,0,$q$7² + 24² = 25², so it's a right triangle with legs 7 and 24. Area = (1/2)(7)(24) = 84.$q$,$j${"2":"Don't forget the 1/2."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000046','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$What is the period of the graph of y = 2 sin(3x)?$q$,$j$["3π","2π","6π","2π/3"]$j$::jsonb,3,$q$The period of sin(bx) is 2π/b = 2π/3. The 2 affects amplitude, not period.$q$,$j${"2":"Divide 2π by 3; don't multiply."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000047','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$In triangle ABC, AB = 8, AC = 5, and the measure of angle A is 60°. What is BC? (Law of cosines: c² = a² + b² − 2ab cos C)$q$,$j$["√129","7","√89","3"]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$BC² = 8² + 5² − 2(8)(5)cos 60° = 64 + 25 − 40 = 49, so BC = 7.$q$,$j${"0":"This adds the cosine term instead of subtracting it.","2":"This leaves out the −2ab cos A term."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000048','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$The radius of a cylinder is doubled and its height is cut in half. The new volume is how many times the original volume?$q$,$j$["1/2","1","2","4"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$V = πr²h. Doubling r multiplies V by 4; halving h multiplies by 1/2. 4 × 1/2 = 2.$q$,$j${"1":"The radius is squared, so doubling it has a bigger effect than halving the height."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000049','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$The points (1, 1), (5, 1), and (5, 4) are the vertices of a triangle in the standard (x, y) coordinate plane. What is the perimeter of the triangle?$q$,$j$["6","10","12","15"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The legs are 4 (horizontal) and 3 (vertical), so the hypotenuse is 5. Perimeter = 4 + 3 + 5 = 12.$q$,$j${"0":"6 is the area."}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b040000-0000-4000-8000-000000000050','ACT',$q$Math$q$,'act-math-geometry',3,null,$q$An arc of a circle with radius 9 has length 6π. What is the measure of the central angle that intercepts the arc?$q$,$j$["40°","60°","120°","240°"]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$Arc length = rθ, so θ = 6π/9 = 2π/3 radians = 120°.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
('5b050000-0001-4000-8000-000000000001','ACT',$q$Reading$q$,'act-reading-key-ideas',1,$q$Passage I — Literary Narrative: This passage is from a short story.

On the last day the shop was open, my grandfather wound every clock in it, though he knew no customer would come to hear them. There were forty-one of them, from the tall walnut case clock by the door to the small brass carriage clocks lined up on the shelf behind the counter, and he went from one to the next with the same unhurried care he had shown them for thirty-eight years.

"They should go out the way they came in," he said when I asked why he bothered. "Running."

I had come to help him pack, but for most of the morning there was little to do except watch. He had sold the building months before, and the new owners planned to open a phone repair store. My mother had told me that Grandpa was relieved to be retiring, that his eyes were no longer good enough for the tiny gears, and that he was looking forward to fishing. But standing in the narrow room, with all the clocks ticking slightly out of step, like a crowd of people talking at once, I wasn't sure she was right.

Around noon a woman came in carrying a shoebox. Inside was a wristwatch with a cracked face. It had been her father's, she said, and it hadn't worked in years. She'd seen the sign in the window and hoped she wasn't too late.

My grandfather looked at the watch for a long moment. Then he cleared a space on the counter, switched on the lamp, and fitted his loupe to his eye. I had seen him do this a thousand times, but I watched now as if for the first time: the way his hands, which shook slightly when he held a coffee cup, became perfectly still over the open watch.

It took him almost an hour. When he finally handed it back, the second hand was sweeping smoothly around the cracked face. The woman tried to pay him, and he waved the money away.

"Last job," he said. "On the house."

After she left, he sat for a while without speaking. Then he stood, took one of the carriage clocks from the shelf, and wrapped it carefully in newspaper.

"For you," he said, placing it in my hands. "You'll have to wind it yourself."$q$,$q$The main purpose of the passage is to:$q$,$j$["explain the technical process of repairing a wristwatch.","describe the history of the building that housed the shop.","depict a significant final day at the grandfather's shop through the narrator's eyes.","argue that phone repair stores are replacing traditional businesses."]$j$::jsonb,2,$q$The passage centers on the shop's last day — winding the clocks, the final repair, the gift — as observed by the narrator.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
