Researchers caution that tardigrades are not indestructible. Active, hydrated tardigrades are far more vulnerable than tuns, and long exposure to high temperatures can kill even dried ones. Still, the mechanisms that allow these tiny animals to survive extreme conditions may someday help scientists preserve vaccines and other medicines without refrigeration.$q$,$q$It can reasonably be inferred from the passage that a hydrated, active tardigrade exposed to strong radiation would be:$q$,$j$["unable to enter the tun state ever again.","less likely to survive than a tardigrade in the tun state.","unaffected by the radiation.","more likely to survive than a tardigrade in the tun state."]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$The passage says active tardigrades are "far more vulnerable than tuns," and the radiation results describe dried tardigrades.$q$,$j${}$j$::jsonb,67,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
