Pill bugs are small land crustaceans. A student studied which conditions pill bugs prefer using a rectangular chamber divided into two equal halves. In each trial, 20 pill bugs were placed in the center of the chamber, and the number of pill bugs in each half was counted after 10 minutes. Each experiment was performed 3 times with new pill bugs.

Experiment 1
One half of the chamber contained dry paper towel; the other contained moist paper towel. Both halves were lit.
Trial: 1 | 2 | 3
Dry half: 4 | 3 | 5
Moist half: 16 | 17 | 15

Experiment 2
Both halves contained moist paper towel. One half was covered to make it dark; the other was lit.
Trial: 1 | 2 | 3
Lit half: 6 | 7 | 5
Dark half: 14 | 13 | 15

Experiment 3
One half was dry and dark; the other half was moist and lit.
Trial: 1 | 2 | 3
Dry and dark half: 9 | 11 | 10
Moist and lit half: 11 | 9 | 10$q$,$q$In Experiment 1, the independent variable was the:$q$,$j$["amount of light in each half of the chamber.","moisture level of each half of the chamber.","length of time before counting.","number of pill bugs counted in each half."]$j$::jsonb,1,$q$Experiment 1 changed whether each half was dry or moist; the counts were the dependent variable.$q$,$j${"3":"The counts are what was measured — the dependent variable."}$j$::jsonb,60,'Original ScoreSpring practice content (AI-drafted; answer keys checked)','ai_generated','approved'),
